[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IRS002
TITLE: Neighbor handoff request, accept, reject, and stale marker
STATEMENT: >>>
The inter-airport interface shall carry a handoff request with aircraft identity and runway intent, an accept, a reject, and a stale marker when the link is down. A receiver shall answer accept or reject. A sender shall treat a down link as stale and shall not send a new request on it. Acceptance is a request followed by accept that transfers control, a reject that does not, and a down link that produces a stale marker and no request.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The neighbor protocol is the only channel whose loss triggers fail-smart behavior.
<<<
DAL: A
REQUIREMENT_LEVEL: Interface
VERIFICATION: Test
ASSUMPTIONS: The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SSS003
